 "lines": [
  {
   "line": "1",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 1.0,
   "end": 6.075,
   "text": "Terribly cold it was, and almost dark — the last evening of the year."
  },
  {
   "line": "2",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 7.0,
   "end": 11.325,
   "text": "A poor little girl shuffled along in her mother's big slippers."
  },
  {
   "line": "3",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 12.0,
   "end": 18.95,
   "text": "Two carriages raced by — she lost them, a boy ran off with one, and now she was barefoot."
  },
  {
   "line": "4",
   "speaker": "GIRL (small, hopeful, to passers-by)",
   "start": 19.3,
   "end": 21.375,
   "text": "Matches… who'll buy my matches?"
  },
  {
   "line": "5",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 21.725,
   "end": 25.3,
   "text": "All day, no one had bought a single match."
  },
  {
   "line": "6",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 25.650000000000002,
   "end": 29.975,
   "text": "Candles gleamed in every window, and it smelled of roast goose."
  },
  {
   "line": "7",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 30.325000000000003,
   "end": 35.775000000000006,
   "text": "She huddled in a corner, afraid to go home: her father would beat her."
  },
  {
   "line": "8",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 36.12500000000001,
   "end": 40.45000000000001,
   "text": "Her hands were numb. If only she dared strike one match…"
  },
  {
   "line": "9",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 41.0,
   "end": 46.075,
   "text": "How it blazed! It was like sitting by a great, warm iron stove."
  },
  {
   "line": "10",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 46.425000000000004,
   "end": 50.37500000000001,
   "text": "Then the flame went out, and the stove was gone."
  },
  {
   "line": "11",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 50.72500000000001,
   "end": 56.17500000000001,
   "text": "She struck another. The wall turned to a veil; inside, a roast goose steamed."
  },
  {
   "line": "12",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 56.52500000000001,
   "end": 61.225000000000016,
   "text": "It hopped down and waddled toward her — and the match went out."
  },
  {
   "line": "13",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 62.0,
   "end": 67.075,
   "text": "With the third, she sat beneath a great Christmas tree, ablaze with candles."
  },
  {
   "line": "14",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 68.0,
   "end": 72.7,
   "text": "It went out. The lights rose up and became stars. One fell."
  },
  {
   "line": "15",
   "speaker": "GIRL (soft, knowing)",
   "start": 73.05,
   "end": 74.375,
   "text": "Someone is dying."
  },
  {
   "line": "16",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 76.0,
   "end": 84.45,
   "text": "Her grandmother, the only one who ever loved her, had told her: when a star falls, a soul goes up to God."
  },
  {
   "line": "17",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 84.8,
   "end": 88.75,
   "text": "One more match — and there stood Grandmother, shining and kind."
  },
  {
   "line": "18",
   "speaker": "GIRL (urgent, tearful)",
   "start": 89.1,
   "end": 91.175,
   "text": "Grandmother! Take me with you!"
  },
  {
   "line": "19",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 91.52499999999999,
   "end": 95.85,
   "text": "She struck the whole bundle at once, to keep her near."
  },
  {
   "line": "20",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 96.19999999999999,
   "end": 104.27499999999999,
   "text": "Grandmother took her in her arms, and they flew up, so high — where there is no cold, no hunger, no fear."
  },
  {
   "line": "21",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 104.62499999999999,
   "end": 110.44999999999999,
   "text": "In the cold dawn sat the little girl, rosy-cheeked and smiling — frozen to death."
  },
  {
   "line": "22",
   "speaker": "PASSER-BY (a woman, quietly)",
   "start": 110.79999999999998,
   "end": 112.87499999999999,
   "text": "She wanted to warm herself."
  },
  {
   "line": "23",
   "speaker": "NARRATOR",
   "start": 113.22499999999998,
   "end": 120.17499999999998,
   "text": "No one knew the beautiful things she had seen, or the joy she had found with her grandmother."
  }
 ]
}